// pfodWeb NOTE: dedicated-hardware pin-exclusion audit, 2026-07-12.
// Board: Olimex "ESP32-C6-EVB" — a real, open-source-hardware industrial
// I/O evaluation board (WiFi6/BLE5/802.15.4, 4x 10A/240VAC relay outputs,
// 4x opto-isolated 5-30VDC digital inputs, onboard user button, UEXT/pUEXT
// expansion headers). Board name + REL1-4/DIN1-4 naming in this variant's
// own pins_arduino.h is an exact match for this product.
//
// Sources consulted (see boardsDetails/esp32/esp32c6/esp32c6-evb/notes.txt
// for the full research trail):
//  - https://github.com/OLIMEX/ESP32-C6-EVB (official open-source-hardware
//    repo, CERN OHL v1.2, KiCad schematics + user manual PDF)
//  - https://www.mouser.com/catalog/specsheets/Olimex_12-4-2023_ESP32-C6-EVB-user-manual.pdf
//    and https://store.comet.bg/download-file.php?id=30743 (mirrored user
//    manual revisions)
//  - https://www.olimex.com/Products/IoT/ESP32-C6/ESP32-C6-EVB/open-source-hardware
//    (product page: confirms 4x relay 10A/240VAC, 4x opto-isolated input
//    5-30VDC, dual UEXT connectors - 0.1" pitch and JST)
//  - https://templates.blakadder.com/ESP32-C6-EVB.html (independent Tasmota
//    community pin table: GPIO9=Button1, GPIO10/11/22/23=Relay1-4,
//    GPIO1/2/3/15=Switch1-4/DIN1-4, GPIO8=Led1 - corroborates this board's
//    own pins_arduino.h exactly)
//
// Per-pin decisions:
//
// GPIO9 (BUT_BUILTIN): KEPT, tagged button. Confirmed onboard user button
// ("Button1" per Tasmota template; user manual). Per playbook section 7a,
// tagged with the restricted set ["digital_input","button"] only - not the
// chip-level default full capability set. Not the board's TX/RX/TX1/RX1
// (16/17/5/4) - no conflict; also not SDA/SCL/SS/MOSI/MISO/SCK (6/7/21/18/
// 20/19) - checked explicitly this session, no alias collision found.
//
// GPIO10/11/22/23 (REL1/REL2/REL3/REL4): KEPT at full chip-level default
// capabilities (digital_input/digital_output/pwm_output). Per playbook
// section 3's explicit relay-outputs KEEP policy ("a relay is a simple
// digital on/off actuator, and controlling it from pfodWeb IS the point of
// using such a board with pfodWeb - do not exclude"). User manual/product
// page confirm 4x 10A/240VAC relay outputs. Each tagged with an
// informational "note" identifying its relay-channel role (not a
// capability restriction - matches the existing waveshare_esp32_s3_relay_6ch
// precedent of leaving relay-drive GPIOs at full default capabilities).
// None of these GPIOs equal TX/RX/SDA/SCL/SS/MOSI/MISO/SCK (16/17/6/7/21/
// 18/20/19) - checked explicitly, no collision.
//
// GPIO1/2/3/15 (DIN1/DIN2/DIN3/DIN4): KEPT but capabilities trimmed to
// ["digital_input"] only (dropping the chip-level default's analog_input/
// digital_output/pwm_output). Confirmed opto-isolated digital inputs
// (5-30VDC per Olimex product page/user manual) - the GPIO pin is wired
// only to an optocoupler's phototransistor output, an input-only signal
// path at the board level even though the chip's own inputOnlyGpios list
// is empty (ESP32-C6 has no input-only-at-silicon pins; this is a
// board-wiring restriction, not a chip restriction - matches the task's
// requested check, confirmed no chip-level input-only conflict). Matches
// playbook section 3's KEEP policy for sensor/status-reading pins ("a
// legitimate pfodWeb data-display use case"). Each tagged with an
// informational "note" identifying its DIN-channel role. None of these
// GPIOs equal TX/RX/SDA/SCL/SS/MOSI/MISO/SCK (16/17/6/7/21/18/20/19) -
// checked explicitly, no collision.
//
// GPIO5/GPIO4 (TX1/RX1): KEPT at chip-level default capabilities, NO
// board.json entry needed (falls through to the full chip-level default
// unmodified). This file's own pins_arduino.h comment brackets TX1/RX1
// together with SDA/SCL/SS/MOSI/MISO/SCK as "available at UEXT and pUEXT"
// - i.e. this is the standard Olimex UEXT/pUEXT general-purpose expansion
// header (UART+I2C+SPI+power), not a UART wired to a specific onboard
// peripheral. Confirmed general-purpose, not dedicated hardware - no
// exclusion warranted. GPIO5/GPIO4 are also aliased A5/A4 (analog) in this
// board's pins_arduino.h, which is expected/harmless (already covered by
// the chip-level default's analog_input capability on those pins) and is
// NOT a primary-UART/bus alias collision - checked explicitly, TX/RX/SDA/
// SCL/SS/MOSI/MISO/SCK are 16/17/6/7/21/18/20/19, none of which equal 4 or 5.
//
// Alias-collision check (explicitly performed, per this session's new
// checklist item): grepped every static-const declaration in this board's
// pins_arduino.h for the primary-UART/bus names build_boards.js
// unconditionally consumes (consts.TX/RX/SDA/SCL/SS/MOSI/MISO/SCK, matched
// by exact identifier name only - see build_boards.js parseEsp32Consts/
// buildEsp32Board ~L541-548). Their values are TX=16, RX=17, SDA=6, SCL=7,
// SS=21, MOSI=18, MISO=20, SCK=19 - NONE of these coincide with GPIO9
// (button), GPIO10/11/22/23 (relays), GPIO1/2/3/15 (DIN), or GPIO5/4
// (TX1/RX1, a DIFFERENT declared name from the primary TX/RX and therefore
// never matched by the parser's exact-name lookup). No contaminating alias
// found; no deletions required.
{
  "boardName": "ESP32C6",
  "displayName": "ESP32-C6 Dev Module",
  "family": "esp32",
  "pwm": { "min": 0, "max": 255, "method": "analogWrite" },
  "dac": {},
  "adc": { "bits": 12, "max": 4095, "defaultRefVolts": "3.3" },
  "inputOnlyGpios": [],
  "connections": ["serial", "ble", "tcp", "http"],
  "pinNotes": {
    "8":  "Must be HIGH or floating on reboot",
    "9":  "Must be HIGH for normal boot",
    "15": "Must be LOW or floating on reboot"
  },
  "chipGpios": {
    "0":  { "capabilities": ["analog_input", "digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "1":  { "capabilities": ["digital_input"], "note": "DIN1 - opto-isolated digital input channel (5-30VDC per Olimex ESP32-C6-EVB user manual/product page)." },
    "2":  { "capabilities": ["digital_input"], "note": "DIN2 - opto-isolated digital input channel (5-30VDC per Olimex ESP32-C6-EVB user manual/product page)." },
    "3":  { "capabilities": ["digital_input"], "note": "DIN3 - opto-isolated digital input channel (5-30VDC per Olimex ESP32-C6-EVB user manual/product page)." },
    "4":  { "capabilities": ["analog_input", "digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "5":  { "capabilities": ["analog_input", "digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "6":  { "capabilities": ["analog_input", "digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "7":  { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "8":  { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "9":  { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "button"] },
    "10": { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"], "note": "REL1 - relay output channel (10A/240VAC per Olimex ESP32-C6-EVB user manual/product page)." },
    "11": { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"], "note": "REL2 - relay output channel (10A/240VAC per Olimex ESP32-C6-EVB user manual/product page)." },
    "14": { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "15": { "capabilities": ["digital_input"], "note": "DIN4 - opto-isolated digital input channel (5-30VDC per Olimex ESP32-C6-EVB user manual/product page)." },
    "16": { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "17": { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "18": { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "19": { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "20": { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "21": { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "22": { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"], "note": "REL3 - relay output channel (10A/240VAC per Olimex ESP32-C6-EVB user manual/product page)." },
    "23": { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"], "note": "REL4 - relay output channel (10A/240VAC per Olimex ESP32-C6-EVB user manual/product page)." }
  }
}
